<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Provisional Government of Schleswig-Holstein</h1><p class="st-meta">1848 CE – 1851 CE · capital Kiel</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Rebel German government set up in Kiel in 1848 to free Schleswig and Holstein from Denmark, which fought the First Schleswig War and lost.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In March 1848, as revolutions spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark's</a> new liberal government moved to tie <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> more closely to the kingdom. German nationalists in the duchies responded by forming a provisional government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiel">Kiel</a> on 24 March, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-hartwig-beseler">Wilhelm Hartwig Beseler</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-frederick-of-noer">Prince Frederick of Noer</a>, claiming both duchies for the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government raised a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a> army and received support from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation</a>, whose troops fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> in 1848-1849. It governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiel">Kiel</a> with the backing of the German-speaking estates, while Danish-minded inhabitants of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> opposed it. Great-power pressure forced Prussia to make peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> in 1850.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Fighting alone, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a> army was defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-isted">Isted</a> (Idstedt) in July 1850. Under pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, the government dissolved in early 1851, and Danish rule was restored. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> Protocol of 1852 confirmed the settlement, but the dispute reignited in the war of 1864.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/provisional-government-of-schleswig-holstein.jpg" alt="Provisional Government of Schleswig-Holstein" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Jon Harald Søby · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Schleswig-Holstein.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1848 CE – 1851 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kiel</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wilhelm Hartwig Beseler, Prince Frederick of Noer</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/denmark">Denmark</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Schleswig-Holstein (1848-1851), Provisorische Regierung</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1850&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-schleswig-holstein" aria-label="Provisional Government of Schleswig-Holstein on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4904 316 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Provisional Government of Schleswig-Holstein lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5224 572L5274 535"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5274 535h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5224 572h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5224 572h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kiel. <a href="/atlas?year=1850&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-schleswig-holstein">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
